{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/397670-how-would-arisen-wage-war-on-each-other","id":397670,"title":"How would Arisen wage war on each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-08T09:35:40-08:00","id":397670,"title":"How would Arisen wage war on each other?","content":"Hi Y'all,<br /> <br /> I just wanted to share my thoughts on how Arisen would wage war on each other, or their enemies. I would imagine that the closest comparison would be to Vampires since both are immortal beings who have influence in the mortal world, as well as powerful abilities. The potential for conflict is great, I wanted to just share how they might go to war with each other when conflict does arise.<br /> <br /> Default conflict: Khent-henu vs. Sedge's Machine: This would be a default conflict in the signature city of DC. Let us assume that, in one corner we have Oba-Heshef, Tarikh-Sethos, and Ur-Qeb. In the other corner we have Sedge, and Bes-Mat (kinda the tough guy, bruiser, Gangrel like figure of DC). Of course, there are many variations to this theme<br /> <br /> First, there are three possibilities for Arisen Warfare<br /> 1/ Both Awake<br /> 2/ Both Asleep<br /> 3/ One is Asleep and the other Awake<br /> <br /> Since Arisen never really die, they can pummel each other to oblivion through the ages and keep coming back. The variable would be how often an Arisen's cult would be able to wake them up. The Cult of the arisen would be the mortal base that vampires rely on so much to fight each other. Strengthening the cult and keeping the cult alive is especially important because Arisen spend so much time asleep. Powers like Eternal Legend are thus very important so that a cult can regenerate itself through the ages.<br /> <br /> So, if destroying an arisen permanently is almost impossible, it might be good to either A/ Target their relics, or B/ Target their cult. How can they do this?<br /> <br /> Raiding another Arisen's cult might be a good idea if you want to destroy their power base. Since a cult is probably no match for an arisen that has just woken up, this can do immense damage to the cult. In addition, an arisen, or group of arisen can raid another tomb for relics. Of course, you then risk waking up the other arisen at the height of their power which would ensure a Sekhem fueled brawl.<br /> <br /> When Arisen go on the offensive there might be some possibilities<br /> 1/ Wake up full of Sekhem, and physically pummel another Arisen who has less Sekhem. Very likely if your cult woke you up because the other mummy was causing them grief<br /> 2/ Guardian Wrath makes for a much more physically powerful Arisen, so does Beast Soul Fury. Enduring Flesh is the equivalent to Resilience in Vampire. Living Monolith makes him tougher overall<br /> 3/ Wake up full of Sekhem, go to the cult of your enemy, slaughter them and take their relics so that they cannot wake up their master<br /> 4/ Use utterances or Affinities that enhance your cult, send them out to raid the other cult. A good example is Gift of the Golden Ankh. <br /> 5/ Use secrets ripped from the skies to target a cult or enemy arisen. A tad unsubtle with a meteor falling out of the sky, but possibly very effective<br /> 6/ Use Dust beneath feet transforms the Arisen into a Mecha like monster<br /> 7/ Lay down Doom Affliction curses, or animals from Beast Master, to harass enemy cult<br /> 8/ Use Word of the Amanuensis to make the enemy cult unable to communicate, makes a very awkward scene<br /> 9/ Awaken the Dead makes some Zombie followers to attack enemy cult<br /> 10/ Words of Dead fury or Words of Dead Glory can make some very nasty ghosts attack your enemies. Bes-Mat has excellent knowledge of these Utterances.<br /> <br /> A key point also seems to be to take away Vessels that belong to your opponent. If you force the enemy cult to permanently drain relics, then their ability to re-awaken their master becomes more difficult. Rite of the Sacred Scarab tier 2 would be an excellent way to ensure that your cult will always have a vessel to wake you up with. This Utterance is probably very good when paired with Eternal Legend, since it would ensure that there is always some cult somewhere that remembers you, and they always have something to wake you up with. <br /> <br /> Anyways, these are just some insane ramblings. Feel free to add or take away what you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T09:53:09-08:00","id":397702,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all, there wouldn't <i>be</i> a Washington DC if there was an Arisen war; Sekhem 10 Mummies that have a reason to get REAL violent tend to destroy large swathes of real estate.<br /> <br /> Go Google &quot;Global War On Mummies&quot;. I dare you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:33:48-08:00","id":397834,"title":"","content":"One of the most important vulnerabilities of a mummy is her memory. Confuse her. Play on her feelings of alienation and detachment. Plant people in her cult who give her false information about the past. Works better and is more interesting than any Utterance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:56:21-08:00","id":397867,"title":"","content":"Most warfare between Arisen will be between their cults - who are unlikely to want to break their Mutually Assured Destruction postures by waking up their deathless masters unless it's necessary. Or unless someone with more ambition or emotional investment in the conflict than sense is in a position to perform the Call, which makes for a great story.<br /> <br /> Look for mortal cultists undermining the assets and cultists of the other cult without recourse to supernatural power. If the Mummy has Eternal Legend then their followers will be more capable as they invoke the Mummy's name to bless otherwise mundane efforts to further their goals. If the Mummy has Dreams of Dead Gods then expect prophetic dreams and mystical obsessions to dominate the behavior of the cultists while directing them to aims that their god desires.<br /> <br /> If the opposing cult has a mummy with Dreams of Dead Gods, good luck with your cultists finding the resolve to interfere with their assets and followers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T14:23:50-08:00","id":398050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/397670-how-would-arisen-wage-war-on-each-other?p=397702#post397702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first of all, there wouldn't <i>be</i> a Washington DC if there was an Arisen war; Sekhem 10 Mummies that have a reason to get REAL violent tend to destroy large swathes of real estate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, most Mummy violence is going to be quite hands-on and not all that likely to level a city. You might get a freak sandstorm or some strange lights in the sky, but Dust Beneath Feet and Secrets Ripped From Skies are the only two capable of causing widespread devastation, and Dust Beneath Feet is a three day ritual that broadcasts the user's location to everything supernatural in the city.<br /> <br /> My own players took a long, long time to wrap their heads around the concept of Mummy violence. In effect, Mummy vs Mummy combat is the <i>least</i> serious, lowest tier of combat. It temporarily inconveniences the one who loses, and that's about it. When you begin to target the more fragile mainstays of Arisen existence, specifically the infrastructure that they require to exist, that's when combat gets heated. Desecrating a tomb, destroying a cult, and stealing the vessels in another Mummy's Lifeweb all imperil a Mummy's continued activity on the stage of eternity. That's when the conflict becomes a big deal. Deliberately messing with a Mummy's purpose is a pretty big deal as well, but more limited in scope. A Mummy failing its purpose means that it has failed in this particular descent, destroying a Cult or Tomb could keep a Mummy from returning for many years to come.<br /> <br /> To actually &quot;kill&quot; a Mummy, you need to do some combination of the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Steal, without awakening the Mummy, their Khat and all Canopic Jars.<br /> 2. Kill every single one of their mortal followers, leaving no one to do the summoning ritual.<br /> 3. Steal every vessel the cult has access to, and prevent them from obtaining any more (probably the hardest due to its requirement of constant vigilance, the prior two allow you to rest a lot more easily for the next few centuries).<br /> <br /> Most Mummy combat is going to operate on a more subtle level than this, because Mummies are inherently vulnerable. They're not awake to monitor their own interests, so I imagine there's a certain... let's call it a gentleman's agreement. The cults can fight and undermine one another, but there should never be a concerted effort to destroy all worship of another Mummy. If you do so, what is to stop others doing it to you? Cultists are mortal and fragile, and you're not there to protect them most of the time. Better to keep the wars confined to movements on the stock market and political scandals, not minor acts of genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}